# Cloudflare Pages rules for the static export (out/).
#
# Only client-routed deep links get 200 rewrites — every real exported page
# (create, asedex/markets, docs/*, admin/*, ...) is a file on disk and
# must never be shadowed by a catch-all. Rewriting to a *.html file or a dir
# path makes Pages answer 308 to the canonical URL, so targets below are
# canonical clean paths of flat html shells emitted by post-export.mjs.
#
# /asepad/token/* and /lock/* point at /_sh/* copies of their placeholder
# shells: a rewrite target inside its own wildcard (/asepad/token/_) loops on
# Pages.
#
# NOTE: Pages does NOT support external 200 proxies (Netlify did) — chain RPC
# calls are relayed by the Pages Function in functions/rpc/, and
# /api/indexer/* by functions/api/indexer/.
# API lanes — the AWS unified API serves every domain; the old Cloudflare
# worker shards are retired. /api/indexer/* goes straight to the explorer
# indexer; everything else lands on AWS (match order matters — specific first).
/api/indexer/*        https://explorer.asentum.com/api/indexer/:splat      302
/api/*                https://api.asepad.fun/api/:splat     302
/favicon.ico          /icon.png              200
/asepad/create        /create                301
/asedex/wallets       /asedex/wallet         301
/asepad/token/*       /_sh/token             200
/lock/*               /_sh/lock              200
/asedex/terminal/*    /asedex/terminal       200
